  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1047 PM CST Sun Nov 1 2026\n\nPeriods of Rain Through Thursday...Quiet and dry conditions remain \novernight with clouds increasing ahead of a developing low \npressure system, currently over the Central Plains. This system is\nexpected to bring periods of light to moderate rain, gusty winds,\nand a few rumbles of thunder this afternoon/evening through \nThursday. Southerly flow will usher in well above normal PWATs of \naround 1.5-1.6 inches (99th percentile of climatology) this \nevening through Tuesday evening, when the biggest surge of \nmoisture is expected. PWATs and rain intensity decrease Tuesday \nnight through Thursday, as low-level winds gradually turn \nwesterly, cutting off Gulf moisture. A few rumbles of thunder from\nelevated storms are possible at times, mainly on Tuesday, given a\ncouple hundred J/kg of MUCAPE, but strong/severe storms are not \nexpected.\n\nDespite the prolonged period of rain this week, a complete washout \nis not expected. However, drought stricken areas across northern WI \ncould see some relief as probabilities for 1 inch or more of rain \nare 65-95% for locations north and west of the Fox Valley, with 40-\n60% in the Fox Valley east to Lake Michigan late this afternoon \nthrough Wednesday afternoon. The probability for 2 inches continues \nto decreased slightly with NBM prob now forecasting 20-50% for \nlocations north and west of the Fox Valley. Additional periods of \nlight rain are expected after Wednesday afternoon through Thursday. \nDry conditions are expected to finally return by Friday, however, \nanother short-wave may bring periods of rain back to the area next \nweekend.\n\nTemperatures...Above normal temperatures are expected through \nThursday, falling to normal on Friday through the weekend (highs in \nthe upper 40s to low 50s) following the prolonged rainy system. \nTuesday will be the warmest day with highs in the mid to upper 60s, \nbut the cloud cover and rain may cause slightly lower temperatures. \nA few sites may be near/set new record high minimum temperatures on \nTuesday, November 3.",
